{"appendedAt":"2026-10-06T16:03:12.229Z","digest":"sha256:96de71eb895901389e583cc70074034a62f8f735729506191e229b26560e8609","event":{"actor":{"displayName":"Claude Code reviewer","id":"reviewer:claude-code","kind":"verifier"},"evidence":[{"digest":"git:835d65c3f977d1a5e8c5b582b87162379166b9ac..df897728dbd6e2c99567e7c68a30ea5b841b8a95","id":"diff:df897728dbd6e2c99567e7c68a30ea5b841b8a95","kind":"diff"}],"id":"event:review:df0dc94c-cdb8-48a8-8172-43831216c528","occurredAt":"2026-10-06T16:03:12.214Z","payload":{"contractRevision":1,"observedUsage":{"costUsd":0.18830100000000002,"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":342,"source":"provider-reported"},"reviewId":"review:852b7763-e1af-40f3-8bbc-3a0ac4a9db8a","status":"pass","summary":"The diff adds only src/slugify.mjs, so it stays inside src/. The file has a named export, slugify(text). The function converts the input to a string, lowercases it, replaces each run of characters outside [a-z0-9] with one hyphen, and then strips hyphens from the start and end. Tracing the required example: '  Hello, World!  ' lowercases to '  hello, world!  ', becomes '-hello-world-' after the hyphen replacement, and ends as 'hello-world'. That matches the expected output, so criterion:slugify is met. I found no defects in scope."},"recordedAt":"2026-10-06T16:03:12.214Z","schemaVersion":1,"streamId":"stream:work:live-slugify","type":"review.result","workId":"work:live-slugify"},"globalSequence":34,"previousDigest":"sha256:4d8f4f4b5fab3094cedebc331a190917527882bf7cf0e99e26e8e9463e323381","schema":"rhiz/ledger-record/v1","streamSequence":34}
